# Directory-size policy for `restsift arch check` / `restsift refactor-scan`
# (allow-listed KEY=value grammar; never executed). Thresholds are the
# restsift defaults. Exempt directories are still measured; `--base` flags
# an exemption whose directory grows notably, so it cannot hide sprawl.
DIR_FILE_WARN_AT=25
DIR_FILE_ERROR_AT=40
DIR_FILE_CRITICAL_AT=70

# Keep-as-is decisions (2026-11-14 review):
# - tests/bash: one bats file per script or feature, each independent; a
#   flat directory is what run-bats.sh, CI and the hygiene test expect.
#   Splitting it changes no behaviour and churns every REPO_ROOT path.
# - home/dot_local/bin: every file is its own command in ~/.local/bin;
#   merging small helpers would remove commands.
# - home/dot_config: chezmoi mirrors ~/.config, so each application decides
#   its own subdirectory; the fan-out is the target layout, not a design.
# ops/ (29 files) is deliberately NOT exempt: it mixes install, update,
# checks and tooling and should be split in its own change.
DIR_FILE_ALLOW=(tests/bash home/dot_local/bin home/dot_config)
